        "market_heading": "Why home staging matters in the Dallas market",
        "market_text": "<p>Dallas–Fort Worth adds more people each year than almost any metro in the country, and a large share of them are relocating on a corporate timeline from California, Illinois or the Northeast. They build a shortlist online weeks before they fly in, and an empty room gives them nothing to judge but square footage.</p><p>The other half of the market is new construction. Plano, Frisco, McKinney and Prosper turn over thousands of spec homes and model-plan builds where six listings in a development share three floor plans. Photographed empty, they're indistinguishable — home staging is what makes one of them the listing a relocating buyer remembers.</p><p>DFW price points also make the maths obvious. Physical staging is priced for furniture plus a monthly rental period regardless of how long the listing sits. Virtual home staging is {price:virtual-staging} a photo, once, with no rental clock — which matters on a builder's inventory of eight vacant homes rather than one.</p>",
